+    \subsection{Covariant vortex-worldsheet form-degree guard}
+        \label{subsec:covariant_vortex_worldsheet_guard}
+
+        \textbf{[ORTHODOX DIFFERENTIAL-FORM GUARD / RESEARCH-TRACK INTERFACE].}
+        A covariant thin-string description may use a two-form potential
+        \(B\in\Omega^2(M)\) and its three-form field strength
+        \begin{align}
+            H=dB\in\Omega^3(M),
+            \qquad
+            H_{\mu\nu\rho}=3\nabla_{[\mu}B_{\nu\rho]},
+            \label{eq:canon_two_form_degree_guard}
+        \end{align}
+        where the brackets have unit-weight antisymmetrization.  A closed
+        two-dimensional string worldsheet \(\Sigma\) may couple electrically through
+        the pullback of \(B\),
+        \begin{align}
+            S_{\Sigma B}=q_B\int_{\Sigma}X^{*}B,
+            \label{eq:canon_worldsheet_B_coupling}
+        \end{align}
+        because both the integration domain and the pulled-back form have degree two.
+        By contrast, \(\int_{S^2}H\) is not a defined flux integral because
+        \(H\) has degree three.  In \(3+1\) dimensions an electric string charge is
+        instead tested by the dual one-form on a loop \(C\simeq S^1\) linking the
+        string,
+        \begin{align}
+            Q_B[C]
+            =
+            \frac{1}{g_B^2}\oint_C {*H},
+            \label{eq:canon_two_form_linking_charge}
+        \end{align}
+        whereas an \(H\)-flux, when the topology supplies a suitable cycle, is
+        integrated over a three-cycle.
+
+        \textbf{[CANON NON-IDENTIFICATION].}
+        Equations~\eqref{eq:canon_two_form_degree_guard}--\eqref{eq:canon_two_form_linking_charge}
+        fix only the covariant bookkeeping.  They do not identify \(q_B\) with the
+        canonical circulation \(\Gamma_0\), do not identify \(B_{\mu\nu}\) with the
+        electromagnetic field, and do not establish that the SST core has already
+        been reduced to a worldsheet EFT.  The corresponding action, scale-separation
+        assumptions, source conservation, reconnection exceptions, and matching gates
+        are confined to Sec.~\ref{sec:rt_covariant_two_form_worldsheet} of the
+        companion Research Track \cite{KalbRamond1974,HornNicolisPenco2015}.
+
